module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.InducedTopology
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.SheafEquiv
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Equivalence
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Over
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Topologies.SpacesEtaleLocalization

/-!
# The slice of the spaces-étale site is the spaces-étale site of the slicing object, as a site

Let `X` be an algebraic space and `U` an algebraic space étale over `X`. The equivalence of
categories `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.sliceEquivSmall` identifies the slice category
`Over U` of the spaces-étale site of `X` with the spaces-étale site of `U`. This file upgrades
that identification to an equivalence of *sites*: the localization at `U` of the topology of
the spaces-étale site of `X` is carried to the topology of the spaces-étale site of `U`, so the
two categories of sheaves agree.

The reduction that makes this cheap is that the comparison is *strict*: the underlying algebraic
space of an object of the slice is literally the underlying algebraic space of its image, and
likewise for morphisms, so `sliceToSmall ⋙ toSpaces` and `Over.forget ⋙ toSpaces` are equal
functors on the nose. Since a family in either site covers exactly when it is jointly surjective
on the points of the underlying algebraic space of its target, the two *precoverages* of the
slice agree with no transport at all. Localizing a topology generated by a precoverage is
generating from the comapped precoverage
(`CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget`), so the comparison of
Grothendieck topologies reduces to that comparison of precoverages.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.sheafOverEquivSmall`: sheaves on the localization at `U`
  of the spaces-étale site of `X` are equivalent to sheaves on the spaces-étale site of `U`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point`: a presieve of
  the spaces-étale site covers exactly when it is jointly surjective on points, with no
  reference to a presenting family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.precoverage_hasIsos`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.precoverage_isStableUnderBaseChange` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.precoverage_isStableUnderComposition`: the three
  stability properties of the precoverage of the spaces-étale site, in the form the localization
  and comparison lemmas ask for.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.sliceToSmall_comp_toSpaces`: the strict comparison, an
  equality of functors on the nose.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.comap_forget_eq_comap_sliceToSmall`: the two precoverages
  of the slice agree.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.topology_over_eq_inducedTopology`: the localization at
  `U` of the topology of the spaces-étale site of `X` is the topology induced along
  `sliceToSmall` by the topology of the spaces-étale site of `U`.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here carries a Stacks attribute. The statement of Tag 0GFS is about sheaves on the small
étale sites of a family of algebraic spaces over `X`; the site equivalence proved here is one of
its two ingredients, the other being a transport of `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData`
along a fibrewise equivalence of pseudofunctors, which is not available. Registering 0GFS on
anything proved here would register it on an instance of Tag 04TS, which already carries that tag
on its general form in
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isEquivalence_toDescentData_pseudofunctorOver`.

`CategoryTheory.Presieve.map_functorPullback_eq_self` is a general fact about a full functor that
is surjective on objects on the nose, and belongs beside Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.map_functorPullback`; it is proved here because that is where it is
needed. The three precoverage stability instances belong beside the precoverage itself in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Topologies.SpacesEtaleSite`, which carries Stacks
attributes and is therefore left unchanged.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GFS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GFS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.Presieve

/-- A presieve on an object in the image of a full functor that is surjective on objects on the
nose is the image of its own pullback. One inclusion is Mathlib's `map_functorPullback`; the
other needs every arrow of the presieve to be the image of an arrow, which is exactly fullness
once the source object is literally in the image. -/
theorem map_functorPullback_eq_self {C : Type*} {D : Type*} [Category C] [Category D]
    (F : C ⥤ D) [F.Full] (hobj : ∀ Y : D, ∃ Z : C, F.obj Z = Y)
    {W : C} (R : Presieve (F.obj W)) :
    Presieve.map F (Presieve.functorPullback F R) = R :=
  le_antisymm (Presieve.map_functorPullback R) (by
    intro Y g hg
    obtain ⟨Z, rfl⟩ := hobj Y
    obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := F.map_surjective g
    exact Presieve.map_map hg)

end CategoryTheory.Presieve

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-! ### The precoverage, characterized without a presenting family -/

/-- A presieve of the spaces-étale site of `X` covers exactly when every point of the underlying
algebraic space of its target is in the image of one of its arrows. This drops the presenting
zero-hypercover from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.mem_precoverage_iff`, which is what
makes the stability properties below readable: a presieve is the family of its own arrows, by
Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Presieve.exists_eq_ofArrows`. -/
theorem mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point {W : SpacesEtale B S hS X}
    {R : Presieve W} :
    R ∈ precoverage B S hS X W ↔
      ∀ x : points B S hS ((toSpaces B S hS X).obj W).1,
        ∃ (Z : SpacesEtale B S hS X) (g : Z ⟶ W), R g ∧
          ∃ y : points B S hS ((toSpaces B S hS X).obj Z).1,
            pointsMap B S hS ((toSpaces B S hS X).obj Z).1
              ((toSpaces B S hS X).map g).hom y = x := by
  rw [mem_precoverage_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ x
    obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hE x
    exact ⟨E.X i, E.f i, E.presieve₀_f i, y, hy⟩
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨ι, Y, f, rfl⟩ := Presieve.exists_eq_ofArrows R
    refine ⟨⟨ι, Y, f⟩, rfl, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨Z, g, ⟨i⟩, y, hy⟩ := h x
    exact ⟨i, y, hy⟩

/-! ### The three stability properties of the precoverage -/

/-- The precoverage of the spaces-étale site of `X` contains the isomorphisms: this is the
isomorphism axiom of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.isSite`, read through the
one-element zero-hypercover. -/
instance precoverage_hasIsos : (precoverage B S hS X).HasIsos where
  mem_coverings_of_isIso f :=
    ⟨PreZeroHypercover.singleton f, (PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_singleton f).symm,
      (isSite B S hS X).1 f⟩

/-- The precoverage of the spaces-étale site of `X` is stable under base change. The projections
of a fibre product in the site are a fibre product of algebraic spaces, because the inclusion
into the slice over `X` and the forgetful functor of the slice both preserve them, and a point of
the base lifts to the fibre product by Tag 03H4. -/
instance precoverage_isStableUnderBaseChange :
    (precoverage B S hS X).IsStableUnderBaseChange where
  mem_coverings_of_isPullback {ι} {S₀} {Xf} f hR {Y} g {P} p₁ p₂ h := by
    rw [mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point] at hR ⊢
    intro y
    obtain ⟨Z, k, ⟨i⟩, z, hz⟩ := hR (pointsMap B S hS _ ((toSpaces B S hS X).map g).hom y)
    obtain ⟨w, hw₁, -⟩ := exists_point_of_isPullback B S hS
      ((h i).map (toSpaces B S hS X)) y z hz.symm
    exact ⟨P i, p₁ i, Presieve.ofArrows.mk i, w, hw₁⟩

/-- The precoverage of the spaces-étale site of `X` is stable under composition: a point of the
target lifts through a member of the outer family and then through a member of the corresponding
inner family. -/
instance precoverage_isStableUnderComposition :
    (precoverage B S hS X).IsStableUnderComposition where
  comp_mem_coverings {ι} {S₀} {Xf} f hf {σ} {Yf} g hg := by
    rw [mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point] at hf ⊢
    intro x
    obtain ⟨Z, k, ⟨i⟩, z, hz⟩ := hf x
    obtain ⟨Z', k', ⟨j⟩, w, hw⟩ := (mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point B S hS).mp (hg i) z
    refine ⟨Yf i j, g i j ≫ f i, Presieve.ofArrows.mk (⟨i, j⟩ : Σ i, σ i), w, ?_⟩
    rw [Functor.map_comp,
      show ((toSpaces B S hS X).map (g i j) ≫ (toSpaces B S hS X).map (f i)).hom
          = ((toSpaces B S hS X).map (g i j)).hom ≫ ((toSpaces B S hS X).map (f i)).hom from rfl,
      congrFun (pointsMap_comp B S hS _ ((toSpaces B S hS X).map (g i j)).hom
      ((toSpaces B S hS X).map (f i)).hom) w]
    simpa only [Function.comp_apply, hw] using hz

/-! ### The two precoverages of the slice agree -/

/-- The image under a functor of a presieve of the source covers exactly when the arrows of the
presieve are jointly surjective on points after the functor. The point of stating it this way is
that the right-hand side mentions the composite with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.toSpaces` and nothing else about the functor. -/
theorem map_mem_precoverage_iff {C : Type*} [Category C] {T : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (F : C ⥤ SpacesEtale B S hS T) {W : C} (R : Presieve W) :
    R.map F ∈ precoverage B S hS T (F.obj W) ↔
      ∀ x : points B S hS ((F ⋙ toSpaces B S hS T).obj W).1,
        ∃ (Z : C) (g : Z ⟶ W), R g ∧
          ∃ y : points B S hS ((F ⋙ toSpaces B S hS T).obj Z).1,
            pointsMap B S hS ((F ⋙ toSpaces B S hS T).obj Z).1
              ((F ⋙ toSpaces B S hS T).map g).hom y = x := by
  rw [mem_precoverage_iff_forall_exists_point]
  constructor
  · intro h x
    obtain ⟨Z, g, ⟨hk⟩, y, hy⟩ := h x
    exact ⟨_, _, hk, y, hy⟩
  · intro h x
    obtain ⟨Z, g, hg, y, hy⟩ := h x
    exact ⟨F.obj Z, F.map g, Presieve.map_map hg, y, hy⟩

/-- Passing from the slice of the spaces-étale site of `X` at `U` to the spaces-étale site of `U`
does not move the underlying algebraic space, nor the underlying morphism of algebraic spaces:
the two composites to algebraic spaces are equal functors, on the nose. -/
theorem sliceToSmall_comp_toSpaces (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) :
    sliceToSmall B S hS U ⋙ toSpaces B S hS U.obj.left
      = Over.forget U ⋙ toSpaces B S hS X := rfl

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.map_mem_precoverage_iff` with the composite to algebraic
spaces supplied as a parameter, so that two functors with the *same* composite give literally the
same criterion. -/
theorem map_mem_precoverage_iff' {C : Type*} [Category C] {T : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (F : C ⥤ SpacesEtale B S hS T) (G : C ⥤ AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hG : F ⋙ toSpaces B S hS T = G) {W : C} (R : Presieve W) :
    R.map F ∈ precoverage B S hS T (F.obj W) ↔
      ∀ x : points B S hS (G.obj W).1,
        ∃ (Z : C) (g : Z ⟶ W), R g ∧
          ∃ y : points B S hS (G.obj Z).1,
            pointsMap B S hS (G.obj Z).1 (G.map g).hom y = x := by
  subst hG
  exact map_mem_precoverage_iff B S hS F R

/-- **The two precoverages of the slice agree.** Pulling the precoverage of the spaces-étale site
of `X` back along the forgetful functor of the slice at `U` gives the same precoverage as pulling
the precoverage of the spaces-étale site of `U` back along `sliceToSmall`, because by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.sliceToSmall_comp_toSpaces` both come out as the same
joint-surjectivity condition on the same algebraic spaces. -/
theorem comap_forget_eq_comap_sliceToSmall (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) :
    (precoverage B S hS X).comap (Over.forget U)
      = (precoverage B S hS U.obj.left).comap (sliceToSmall B S hS U) :=
  Precoverage.ext (funext fun _ ↦ Set.ext fun R ↦
    (map_mem_precoverage_iff' B S hS (Over.forget U) _ rfl R).trans
      (map_mem_precoverage_iff' B S hS (sliceToSmall B S hS U) _
        (sliceToSmall_comp_toSpaces B S hS U) R).symm)

/-! ### The equivalence of sites -/

/-- `sliceToSmall` is surjective on objects on the nose: the round trip through `smallToSlice`
returns the object it started from, not merely an isomorphic one. This is the object half of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.smallToSlice_comp_sliceToSmall`. -/
theorem sliceToSmall_obj_surjective (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X)
    (V : SpacesEtale B S hS U.obj.left) :
    ∃ W : Over U, (sliceToSmall B S hS U).obj W = V :=
  ⟨(smallToSlice B S hS U).obj V, rfl⟩

/-- The functor `sliceToSmall` from the slice of the spaces-étale site of `X` at `U` to the
spaces-étale site of `U` is an equivalence of categories. -/
instance sliceToSmall_isEquivalence (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) :
    (sliceToSmall B S hS U).IsEquivalence :=
  (sliceEquivSmall B S hS U).isEquivalence_functor

/-- **`sliceEquivSmall` is an equivalence of sites.** The localization at `U` of the topology of
the spaces-étale site of `X` is the topology induced along `sliceToSmall` by the topology of the
spaces-étale site of `U`.

The localization of a topology generated by a precoverage is generated by the comapped
precoverage; the two comapped precoverages agree; and for a full, faithful functor that is
surjective on objects on the nose, generating from a comapped precoverage gives the restricted
topology, which for an equivalence is the induced one. -/
theorem topology_over_eq_inducedTopology (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) :
    (topology B S hS X).over U
      = (sliceToSmall B S hS U).inducedTopology (topology B S hS U.obj.left) := by
  rw [over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget,
    comap_forget_eq_comap_sliceToSmall,
    Precoverage.toGrothendieck_comap_eq_restrictedTopology (sliceToSmall B S hS U)
      (precoverage B S hS U.obj.left)
      (fun {_} {R} hR ↦ by
        rwa [Presieve.map_functorPullback_eq_self _ (sliceToSmall_obj_surjective B S hS U) R]),
    Functor.restrictedTopology_eq_inducedTopology]

/-- The functor `sliceToSmall` exhibits the slice of the spaces-étale site of `X` at `U`, with the
localized topology, as a dense subsite of the spaces-étale site of `U`. -/
instance isDenseSubsite_sliceToSmall (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) :
    (sliceToSmall B S hS U).IsDenseSubsite ((topology B S hS X).over U)
      (topology B S hS U.obj.left) := by
  rw [topology_over_eq_inducedTopology]
  infer_instance

/-- **Sheaves on the slice of the spaces-étale site of `X` at `U` are sheaves on the spaces-étale
site of `U`.** This is the comparison lemma at the dense subsite
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale.isDenseSubsite_sliceToSmall`. -/
noncomputable def sheafOverEquivSmall (U : SpacesEtale B S hS X) (A : Type*) [Category A]
    [∀ Y, HasLimitsOfShape (StructuredArrow Y (sliceToSmall B S hS U).op) A] :
    Sheaf ((topology B S hS X).over U) A ≌ Sheaf (topology B S hS U.obj.left) A :=
  Functor.IsDenseSubsite.sheafEquiv _ _ (sliceToSmall B S hS U) A

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SpacesEtale

end
